  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water, Land and Roads Investment Program - Year 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Welfare Association (Taawon), a leading development organization in Palestine, in partnership with the Land Research Center (LRC), and the Palestinian Hydrological Group (PHG), is leading and implementing the Water, Land, and Agricultural Roads Investment Program funded by the Dutch Representative Office (NRO) in Ramallah. The overall goal of the program is to achieve &#x201c;increased resilience, resource use efficiency, sustainable food production and productivity for Palestinian agricultural producers and their organizations,&#x201d; and the purpose of the program is &#x201c;sustainable access to water and land productivity, enhancing farm household income, advanced capabilities, and agricultural and climate practices for small farming families, agricultural producers and their organizations in the targeted locations in the West Bank.</narrative>
  </description>
